 "notes": "Stretch 2. p.103 Ani text starts below the short rule at y≈530 with the overlined title '1. Re en seset nifu …'; p.105 stops at 'Ani em maāχeru' (y≈530), above the rule before Chapter XLIV. Line numerals, LVIII: 1. before Re (p.103 title row, left margin); 2. inside χeper - nek between D21 and N35/V31 (p.103 row 3); 3. between em and teken (p.103 row 4, right end); 4. between baiu and ren (p.103 last row); 5. inside mat'abet after the owl group (p.104 row 1, right end); 6. between qeres - k - tu and em (p.104 row 3); 7. inside àuf before its flesh det (p.104 row 4). LIX: 1. before Re (p.104 title); 2. between mu (?) and nifu (p.104 last row); 3. between sau - nà and suḥt (p.105 row 1); 4. between ānχ - à and seset - s (p.105 row 2). No numeral on p.104 row 8 (t'eṭ àn … em). Overlines: LVIII title Re…second em (Neter - χert not overlined); p.104 row 5 overline begins over àr and runs to the line end (àr reχ re pen àu - f āq - f emχet); continues on row 6 over pert em only (neter - χert ent not overlined); LIX title Re…second em (Neter-χert not overlined); p.104 row 8 short overline over t'eṭ àn only. Budge's English dots: under setut ('likewise ........') and the whole of qeres - k - tu ('................') — recorded as printed. Budge prints '(sic)' after ṭeni, '(?)' after mu on p.104. Several words (t'eṭ àn / er) have no English of their own; gloss left empty. A raised tick after baiu on p.103 looks like a footnote mark but no footnote is printed on the page."
